SAMPLES/INIT - start diablo and dreaderd with the init system of the machine

These are thin wrappers: every one calls samples/adm/diablo-ctl (installed as
/news/adm/diablo-ctl), which does the starting, stopping, status and checks,
reads its settings from diablo-ctl.conf (see samples/adm/diablo-ctl.conf) and
only ever touches its own site.  Edit the options of the daemons there (-p
pathhost and so on), never in a wrapper.

The wrappers assume the install prefix /news.  With another PREFIX replace
/news/adm/diablo-ctl (and /news/log/*.pid in the systemd units) by yours, and
give diablo-ctl "-C <prefix>/diablo.config" (put it into the ExecStart and
ExecStop lines, the SMF exec attributes, diablo_flags in rc.conf, or
DIABLO_CTL_OPTS): the programs read /news/diablo.config unless they are told
another, and that file needs "path_home <prefix>".  Without -C a second site's
wrapper would start, stop and check the site in /news.

  systemd/diablo.service, dreaderd.service
		Linux with systemd: copy to /etc/systemd/system, then
		    systemctl daemon-reload
		    systemctl enable --now diablo       (and/or dreaderd)
		Use "systemctl edit" for a spool on its own file system:
		RequiresMountsFor=/news/spool

  freebsd/diablo, dreaderd
		FreeBSD rc.d: copy to /usr/local/etc/rc.d (mode 555), then
		    sysrc diablo_enable=YES dreaderd_enable=YES
		    service diablo start
		"service diablo check" runs the checks without starting.
		Settings in rc.conf: diablo_ctl (path of diablo-ctl) and
		diablo_flags (its options, for example "-f /news/diablo-ctl.conf").

  smf/diablo.xml, dreaderd.xml
		illumos and SmartOS: edit the paths if needed, then
		    svccfg import diablo.xml
		    svcadm enable site/diablo
		The daemons run in the service's contract: when they all die,
		SMF restarts the service.

  sysv/diablo, dreaderd
		SysV init (Debian without systemd, Devuan, old systems): copy to
		/etc/init.d, chmod 755, then update-rc.d diablo defaults (or
		your system's tool).  Settings in /etc/default/diablo:
		DIABLO_CTL and DIABLO_CTL_OPTS.

Order: on a machine with both, diablo starts first and dreaderd stops first (the
reader may fetch articles from the feeder).  The checks that run before a start
(mounts, history, active file, unclean shutdown guard) are explained in
diablo-ctl.conf; "diablo-ctl check" runs them by hand.
